1
00:00:00,290 --> 00:00:02,590
If your knee replacement
still hurts

2
00:00:02,590 --> 00:00:05,090
and the X-ray keeps coming
back fine,

3
00:00:05,090 --> 00:00:06,580
don't accept that.

4
00:00:06,580 --> 00:00:09,010
I've hung drywall for
thirty-one years.

5
00:00:09,010 --> 00:00:09,820
Squatting,

6
00:00:09,820 --> 00:00:10,690
kneeling,

7
00:00:10,690 --> 00:00:11,750
up and down ladders and

8
00:00:11,750 --> 00:00:13,410
stilts all day long.

9
00:00:13,410 --> 00:00:14,420
I had my right knee

10
00:00:14,420 --> 00:00:16,060
replaced two years ago.

11
00:00:16,060 --> 00:00:18,280
It has hurt every day
since.

12
00:00:18,280 --> 00:00:19,740
Not surgery pain.

13
00:00:19,740 --> 00:00:21,250
I know what that felt
like,

14
00:00:21,250 --> 00:00:22,220
and it went away.

15
00:00:22,220 --> 00:00:23,180
This is different.

16
00:00:23,180 --> 00:00:23,860
Tight.

17
00:00:23,860 --> 00:00:24,410
Full.

18
00:00:24,410 --> 00:00:25,500
Like a band around

19
00:00:25,500 --> 00:00:27,270
the joint that never
loosens.

20
00:00:27,270 --> 00:00:28,290
And for two years

21
00:00:28,290 --> 00:00:29,990
I've been told the same
thing.

22
00:00:29,990 --> 00:00:31,120
Give it time.

23
00:00:31,120 --> 00:00:33,160
At six weeks it was
swelling,

24
00:00:33,160 --> 00:00:34,690
and swelling is normal.

25
00:00:34,690 --> 00:00:35,480
At three months,

26
00:00:35,480 --> 00:00:36,690
give it six.

27
00:00:36,690 --> 00:00:37,650
At six months,

28
00:00:37,650 --> 00:00:39,600
some knees take a full
year.

29
00:00:39,600 --> 00:00:40,610
At a year,

30
00:00:40,610 --> 00:00:42,830
eighteen months isn't
unusual.

31
00:00:42,830 --> 00:00:44,250
And I didn't just wait.

32
00:00:44,250 --> 00:00:45,540
We went down the list.

33
00:00:45,540 --> 00:00:47,380
More physical therapy.

34
00:00:47,380 --> 00:00:48,540
Every session,

35
00:00:48,540 --> 00:00:50,210
every exercise at home.

36
00:00:50,210 --> 00:00:51,490
I got stronger.

37
00:00:51,490 --> 00:00:53,270
The tightness never moved.

38
00:00:53,270 --> 00:00:54,760
The pain pills helped,

39
00:00:54,760 --> 00:00:56,210
and that was the problem.

40
00:00:56,210 --> 00:00:58,050
I'm already on enough
every morning,

41
00:00:58,050 --> 00:00:59,130
and nobody could tell me

42
00:00:59,130 --> 00:01:00,550
when I'd get to stop.

43
00:01:00,550 --> 00:01:02,110
Then a nerve block.

44
00:01:02,110 --> 00:01:04,670
Then talk of burning the
nerve.

45
00:01:04,670 --> 00:01:06,250
And after that, a second

46
00:01:06,250 --> 00:01:07,380
operation to go back

47
00:01:07,380 --> 00:01:09,200
in and do it over.

48
00:01:09,200 --> 00:01:10,380
I said no.

49
00:01:10,380 --> 00:01:11,800
Every morning I climbed

50
00:01:11,800 --> 00:01:12,350
out of the truck

51
00:01:12,350 --> 00:01:13,180
at the job

52
00:01:13,180 --> 00:01:14,140
and my knee felt like

53
00:01:14,140 --> 00:01:15,760
a band was wrapped around
it,

54
00:01:15,760 --> 00:01:18,280
tightening every inch I
tried to straighten.

55
00:01:18,280 --> 00:01:20,060
Every morning I took
something

56
00:01:20,060 --> 00:01:21,740
for it and went to work.

57
00:01:21,740 --> 00:01:23,280
Couldn't do the stairs,

58
00:01:23,280 --> 00:01:24,440
couldn't stand at the
counter

59
00:01:24,440 --> 00:01:26,310
long enough to finish
dinner,

60
00:01:26,310 --> 00:01:27,960
couldn't sit through my
granddaughter's

61
00:01:27,960 --> 00:01:30,710
game without shifting
every two minutes.

62
00:01:30,710 --> 00:01:31,960
The young guys on my crew

63
00:01:31,960 --> 00:01:32,690
started taping

64
00:01:32,690 --> 00:01:34,030
the low seams for me.

65
00:01:34,030 --> 00:01:35,560
Nobody said anything.

66
00:01:35,560 --> 00:01:37,000
They didn't have to.

67
00:01:37,000 --> 00:01:38,210
It woke me at night,

68
00:01:38,210 --> 00:01:40,180
and it turned ordinary
things,

69
00:01:40,180 --> 00:01:41,320
like getting in the truck

70
00:01:41,320 --> 00:01:42,690
or up off a bucket,

71
00:01:42,690 --> 00:01:44,060
into a decision.

72
00:01:44,060 --> 00:01:45,300
After a long and serious

73
00:01:45,300 --> 00:01:46,340
talk with my wife,

74
00:01:46,340 --> 00:01:48,290
I went back in one more
time.

75
00:01:48,290 --> 00:01:49,480
That was the fourth set

76
00:01:49,480 --> 00:01:51,340
of X-rays on this knee.

77
00:01:51,340 --> 00:01:52,900
And like the three before
it,

78
00:01:52,900 --> 00:01:55,400
the answer was everything
looks great.

79
00:01:55,400 --> 00:01:57,990
No loosening, no
infection,

80
00:01:57,990 --> 00:01:59,190
nothing wrong.

81
00:01:59,190 --> 00:02:00,550
Only this time there

82
00:02:00,550 --> 00:02:01,810
was no new number.

83
00:02:01,810 --> 00:02:03,040
Nobody said

84
00:02:03,040 --> 00:02:04,840
give it another six
months.

85
00:02:04,840 --> 00:02:06,450
There was nothing left to
give it.

86
00:02:06,450 --> 00:02:07,400
I sat in the parking

87
00:02:07,400 --> 00:02:08,410
lot for a while.

88
00:02:08,410 --> 00:02:09,580
Okay, I thought.

89
00:02:09,580 --> 00:02:11,130
Then explain this.

90
00:02:11,130 --> 00:02:13,010
Anyway, a couple of months
back,

91
00:02:13,010 --> 00:02:14,320
I hit my breaking point.

92
00:02:14,320 --> 00:02:16,190
It was around 2:30 in the
morning.

93
00:02:16,190 --> 00:02:16,930
I had a job

94
00:02:16,930 --> 00:02:18,530
to start at seven.

95
00:02:18,530 --> 00:02:20,430
Everyone in the house was
asleep

96
00:02:20,430 --> 00:02:22,100
and I was downstairs in
the recliner

97
00:02:22,100 --> 00:02:23,220
with my leg up,

98
00:02:23,220 --> 00:02:25,060
trying to find any angle
where

99
00:02:25,060 --> 00:02:26,070
it didn't feel like
something

100
00:02:26,070 --> 00:02:27,540
was wrapped around my knee

101
00:02:27,540 --> 00:02:28,560
and tightening.

102
00:02:28,560 --> 00:02:30,750
My wife didn't know I'd
come downstairs.

103
00:02:30,750 --> 00:02:32,580
By then I'd stopped
telling her.

104
00:02:32,580 --> 00:02:33,770
And I just thought,

105
00:02:33,770 --> 00:02:35,380
is this really my life
now?

106
00:02:35,380 --> 00:02:36,900
I can't live like this.

107
00:02:36,900 --> 00:02:38,560
So I made myself a
promise.

108
00:02:38,560 --> 00:02:39,480
I wouldn't go a day

109
00:02:39,480 --> 00:02:41,220
without looking for an
answer.

110
00:02:41,220 --> 00:02:42,550
And when I found one,

111
00:02:42,550 --> 00:02:43,650
I'd share it with everyone

112
00:02:43,650 --> 00:02:45,460
going through the same
thing.

113
00:02:45,460 --> 00:02:46,440
So I got my laptop

114
00:02:46,440 --> 00:02:47,770
out and went looking.

115
00:02:47,770 --> 00:02:49,070
Not for a product.

116
00:02:49,070 --> 00:02:50,550
For an explanation.

117
00:02:50,550 --> 00:02:52,390
Mayo Clinic forums,

118
00:02:52,390 --> 00:02:54,980
the knee replacement group
on Facebook,

119
00:02:54,980 --> 00:02:58,430
doctor videos, medical
animations.

120
00:02:58,430 --> 00:02:59,710
And that's when I found

121
00:02:59,710 --> 00:03:01,890
a video from a physical
therapist

122
00:03:01,890 --> 00:03:02,680
named Dr.

123
00:03:02,680 --> 00:03:05,360
Steven Salinger, whose own
wife

124
00:03:05,360 --> 00:03:07,360
had been through exactly
this.

125
00:03:07,360 --> 00:03:08,960
But before I say anything
else,

126
00:03:08,960 --> 00:03:11,220
I want to be straight with
you.

127
00:03:11,220 --> 00:03:13,520
You've already had
something work fast.

128
00:03:13,520 --> 00:03:14,570
The ice.

129
00:03:14,570 --> 00:03:16,400
The first week of a new
pill.

130
00:03:16,400 --> 00:03:17,880
The good day after a
session.

131
00:03:17,880 --> 00:03:19,460
Then it wore off.

132
00:03:19,460 --> 00:03:21,820
That's the part nobody
warns you about.

133
00:03:21,820 --> 00:03:23,680
Fast relief isn't relief.

134
00:03:23,680 --> 00:03:25,020
It's a preview.

135
00:03:25,020 --> 00:03:26,430
So I'm not going to tell

136
00:03:26,430 --> 00:03:28,440
you this works fast.

137
00:03:28,440 --> 00:03:29,430
It doesn't.

138
00:03:29,430 --> 00:03:31,190
But if you're willing to
be patient,

139
00:03:31,190 --> 00:03:32,040
and to look at what's

140
00:03:32,040 --> 00:03:33,560
going on around your new
knee

141
00:03:33,560 --> 00:03:35,270
instead of inside it,
there

142
00:03:35,270 --> 00:03:38,220
is a real reason it still
hurts.

143
00:03:38,220 --> 00:03:40,270
And something you can do
about it.

144
00:03:40,270 --> 00:03:41,380
Let me explain what he
said,

145
00:03:41,380 --> 00:03:42,590
because this is what
changed

146
00:03:42,590 --> 00:03:43,970
everything for me.

147
00:03:43,970 --> 00:03:45,810
He started with the
basics.

148
00:03:45,810 --> 00:03:47,330
A knee replacement takes
out

149
00:03:47,330 --> 00:03:49,130
the worn joint surfaces
and puts

150
00:03:49,130 --> 00:03:50,730
in metal and plastic.

151
00:03:50,730 --> 00:03:52,440
That's what stops the
arthritis pain

152
00:03:52,440 --> 00:03:54,210
you had before the
operation.

153
00:03:54,210 --> 00:03:56,170
That part I already knew.

154
00:03:56,170 --> 00:03:57,330
But then he explained
something

155
00:03:57,330 --> 00:03:58,810
nobody had ever told me.

156
00:03:58,810 --> 00:03:59,500
He said,

157
00:03:59,500 --> 00:04:00,960
think about a swollen foot

158
00:04:00,960 --> 00:04:02,080
inside a shoe.

159
00:04:02,080 --> 00:04:03,750
The shoe didn't shrink.

160
00:04:03,750 --> 00:04:05,710
Your foot is taking up
more room,

161
00:04:05,710 --> 00:04:07,170
so everything feels
cramped

162
00:04:07,170 --> 00:04:09,170
and tight and squeezed.

163
00:04:09,170 --> 00:04:10,350
Your new knee sits

164
00:04:10,350 --> 00:04:12,310
in a limited space with
living

165
00:04:12,310 --> 00:04:14,500
tissue packed all around
it.

166
00:04:14,500 --> 00:04:16,390
To put that knee in, the
surgeon

167
00:04:16,390 --> 00:04:18,270
had to work through that
tissue.

168
00:04:18,270 --> 00:04:21,010
Afterwards it gets
inflamed and swollen.

169
00:04:21,010 --> 00:04:22,590
At first that's normal.

170
00:04:22,590 --> 00:04:24,230
But in some people that
swelling can

171
00:04:24,230 --> 00:04:27,120
stay switched on far
longer than expected.

172
00:04:27,120 --> 00:04:28,760
And swollen tissue takes
up more

173
00:04:28,760 --> 00:04:30,750
room than calm tissue
does.

174
00:04:30,750 --> 00:04:32,060
So when you bend,

175
00:04:32,060 --> 00:04:33,840
that tissue gets
compressed.

176
00:04:33,840 --> 00:04:35,020
When you straighten,

177
00:04:35,020 --> 00:04:36,440
it gets pulled tight.

178
00:04:36,440 --> 00:04:37,510
That's the band.

179
00:04:37,510 --> 00:04:39,810
That's the ache that never
quite leaves.

180
00:04:39,810 --> 00:04:40,650
And you start being

181
00:04:40,650 --> 00:04:41,340
the one who says,

182
00:04:41,340 --> 00:04:42,390
you go ahead.

183
00:04:42,390 --> 00:04:43,600
I'll stay here.

184
00:04:43,600 --> 00:04:45,290
And that's exactly why so
much

185
00:04:45,290 --> 00:04:47,440
of what I'd tried hadn't
worked.

186
00:04:47,440 --> 00:04:49,110
Physical therapy
strengthens the muscles

187
00:04:49,110 --> 00:04:50,230
around the knee.

188
00:04:50,230 --> 00:04:51,240
Worth doing,

189
00:04:51,240 --> 00:04:52,260
and I'd done it.

190
00:04:52,260 --> 00:04:53,570
It does nothing about
tissue

191
00:04:53,570 --> 00:04:54,880
taking up room.

192
00:04:54,880 --> 00:04:56,110
A nerve block quiets

193
00:04:56,110 --> 00:04:57,990
the nerve carrying the
signal.

194
00:04:57,990 --> 00:05:00,470
It doesn't touch what's
generating it.

195
00:05:00,470 --> 00:05:02,090
But when that irritated
tissue

196
00:05:02,090 --> 00:05:03,600
finally calms down,

197
00:05:03,600 --> 00:05:05,090
it holds less fluid,

198
00:05:05,090 --> 00:05:07,030
and it takes up less room.

199
00:05:07,030 --> 00:05:08,860
Less room taken up means

200
00:05:08,860 --> 00:05:11,220
less pressure squeezing
the joint.

201
00:05:11,220 --> 00:05:13,380
That's what takes the
pressure off.

202
00:05:13,380 --> 00:05:14,920
After two years of this,

203
00:05:14,920 --> 00:05:16,870
it finally made sense.

204
00:05:16,870 --> 00:05:18,920
The problem was never the
new knee.

205
00:05:18,920 --> 00:05:20,890
It was the tissue crowded
around it.

206
00:05:20,890 --> 00:05:22,690
He calls it the squeeze.

207
00:05:22,690 --> 00:05:25,340
Once you've felt it,
that's the word.

208
00:05:25,340 --> 00:05:26,970
I'd bought knee pads,

209
00:05:26,970 --> 00:05:28,360
knee sleeves,

210
00:05:28,360 --> 00:05:30,720
compression braces,
creams,

211
00:05:30,720 --> 00:05:32,320
half of Amazon really,

212
00:05:32,320 --> 00:05:33,380
and all any of it gave me

213
00:05:33,380 --> 00:05:34,530
was an hour.

214
00:05:34,530 --> 00:05:35,470
I even looked at going

215
00:05:35,470 --> 00:05:37,510
to a clinic for the light
therapy.

216
00:05:37,510 --> 00:05:39,190
But at $200 a session

217
00:05:39,190 --> 00:05:40,980
with nothing covered by
insurance,

218
00:05:40,980 --> 00:05:43,010
that was a quick no.

219
00:05:43,010 --> 00:05:43,930
Then one night I went

220
00:05:43,930 --> 00:05:45,210
back to that knee
replacement

221
00:05:45,210 --> 00:05:46,760
group and actually read
it.

222
00:05:46,760 --> 00:05:48,120
Thousands of people,

223
00:05:48,120 --> 00:05:49,860
years out from surgery,

224
00:05:49,860 --> 00:05:52,070
comparing notes on
stiffness and tightness

225
00:05:52,070 --> 00:05:53,560
nobody could explain.

226
00:05:53,560 --> 00:05:55,290
And no matter how far I
scrolled,

227
00:05:55,290 --> 00:05:57,140
the same thing kept coming
up.

228
00:05:57,140 --> 00:05:58,770
This one device,

229
00:05:58,770 --> 00:06:00,770
and people saying it was
the first

230
00:06:00,770 --> 00:06:02,110
thing that made a
difference.

231
00:06:02,110 --> 00:06:04,280
And before anyone jumps in
thinking,

232
00:06:04,280 --> 00:06:05,330
alright, here it comes,

233
00:06:05,330 --> 00:06:06,390
he's selling me something,

234
00:06:06,390 --> 00:06:08,250
let me shut that down
right now.

235
00:06:08,250 --> 00:06:10,080
I'm only here because I
made myself

236
00:06:10,080 --> 00:06:12,230
a promise at 2:30 in the
morning

237
00:06:12,230 --> 00:06:13,190
that if I ever found

238
00:06:13,190 --> 00:06:14,400
something that helped,

239
00:06:14,400 --> 00:06:15,480
I'd say so.

240
00:06:15,480 --> 00:06:16,790
It's called the KenRelief
Red

241
00:06:16,790 --> 00:06:18,430
Light Therapy Wrap.

242
00:06:18,430 --> 00:06:20,640
At first glance I didn't
buy it.

243
00:06:20,640 --> 00:06:21,610
It looked like the cheap

244
00:06:21,610 --> 00:06:23,000
knee sleeves off Amazon

245
00:06:23,000 --> 00:06:24,630
that did nothing for me.

246
00:06:24,630 --> 00:06:26,280
But I went to their
website anyway,

247
00:06:26,280 --> 00:06:27,200
just to see what all

248
00:06:27,200 --> 00:06:28,630
the fuss was about.

249
00:06:28,630 --> 00:06:30,370
It's the same red light
therapy

250
00:06:30,370 --> 00:06:33,140
clinics charge $200 a
session

251
00:06:33,140 --> 00:06:35,210
for, off machines that
cost

252
00:06:35,210 --> 00:06:36,860
fifty thousand dollars,

253
00:06:36,860 --> 00:06:38,010
in a wrap you plug

254
00:06:38,010 --> 00:06:39,600
into the wall at home.

255
00:06:39,600 --> 00:06:41,540
Two hundred and forty
lights.

256
00:06:41,540 --> 00:06:43,530
Red at 660 nanometers

257
00:06:43,530 --> 00:06:46,040
and near-infrared at 850,

258
00:06:46,040 --> 00:06:48,310
run together for the
strongest effect.

259
00:06:48,310 --> 00:06:49,720
Four strength levels.

260
00:06:49,720 --> 00:06:51,650
A five to thirty minute
timer.

261
00:06:51,650 --> 00:06:53,370
Then I saw the guarantee.

262
00:06:53,370 --> 00:06:54,740
Ninety days.

263
00:06:54,740 --> 00:06:57,040
Results or your money
back,

264
00:06:57,040 --> 00:06:59,240
no questions, no store
credit,

265
00:06:59,240 --> 00:07:00,970
and you don't even send it
back.

266
00:07:00,970 --> 00:07:02,980
No physical therapist ever
gave me ninety

267
00:07:02,980 --> 00:07:04,770
days to change my mind.

268
00:07:04,770 --> 00:07:06,480
There wasn't much to lose,

269
00:07:06,480 --> 00:07:07,550
so I ordered it.

270
00:07:07,550 --> 00:07:09,080
Two of them, actually.

271
00:07:09,080 --> 00:07:11,090
Only the right knee was
replaced,

272
00:07:11,090 --> 00:07:13,200
but you favor the leg that
hurts,

273
00:07:13,200 --> 00:07:14,110
and I'd done it on

274
00:07:14,110 --> 00:07:16,250
every job for two years.

275
00:07:16,250 --> 00:07:18,640
The left one was carrying
the difference.

276
00:07:18,640 --> 00:07:19,900
When it came,

277
00:07:19,900 --> 00:07:22,750
I strapped it on expecting
nothing,

278
00:07:22,750 --> 00:07:24,050
because I'd been let down
too

279
00:07:24,050 --> 00:07:25,800
many times to get excited.

280
00:07:25,800 --> 00:07:27,380
What I felt was warmth.

281
00:07:27,380 --> 00:07:29,310
Not a heating pad kind of
hot.

282
00:07:29,310 --> 00:07:30,890
More like it was coming
from inside

283
00:07:30,890 --> 00:07:32,570
the knee and spreading
around it.

284
00:07:32,570 --> 00:07:33,790
And that was it.

285
00:07:33,790 --> 00:07:35,760
That was the whole
experience.

286
00:07:35,760 --> 00:07:36,960
When I took it off,

287
00:07:36,960 --> 00:07:37,660
I'll be honest,

288
00:07:37,660 --> 00:07:39,480
nothing dramatic had
happened.

289
00:07:39,480 --> 00:07:41,140
And after what that video
said,

290
00:07:41,140 --> 00:07:43,470
that's exactly what I
expected.

291
00:07:43,470 --> 00:07:44,290
What was different

292
00:07:44,290 --> 00:07:46,010
was that for the first

293
00:07:46,010 --> 00:07:47,110
time in two years

294
00:07:47,110 --> 00:07:49,140
I'd done something for my
knee

295
00:07:49,140 --> 00:07:50,800
instead of to it.

296
00:07:50,800 --> 00:07:51,910
Twenty minutes,

297
00:07:51,910 --> 00:07:53,270
